Dreaming OS standalone web root
================================

This directory is installed by the `dreamingwrt-web` package and served by
dreamingwrt-webd/jmxd. It is intentionally separate from LuCI resources.

Layout:

- `index.html`: thin root entry for the new web UI and first-run welcome flow.
- `login/`: temporary standalone login entry while the new SPA grows.
- `static/css`, `static/js`: shared hashed or versioned frontend assets.
- `static/images/logo`: canonical public root for database-mapped application,
  device, brand and carrier logos. The bulk of that catalog is installed by the
  optional `jmxd` logo component, whose filename mapping lives in
  `dreamingwrt_signatures.db`. That component and database are private and are
  **not** part of the public source release, so in a stock public build this
  directory only holds the assets checked into the tree. Frontend code must treat
  a missing logo as normal and fall back to a generic icon.
- `static/images`: Dreaming OS shell identity assets such as
  `dreamingwrt.png` and `logo-64.png`, plus setup artwork and other Web-owned
  images. Shell identity must not depend on the database-mapped logo catalog.
- `static/fonts`: bundled fonts if needed later.
- `static/data`: static JSON dictionaries/manifests.
- `plugins/native`: native Dreaming OS plugin frontend bundles.
- `plugins/third-party`: third-party plugin frontend bundles.
- `dynamic`: read-only runtime files generated or linked by webd/jmxd.
- `assets`: compatibility bucket for assets that have not been classified yet.

Do not add new top-level `/www/foo` directories for the standalone UI. New
frontend code should live under `/www/dreamingwrt` and be installed through this
package so firmware builds remain reproducible.

Shared theme/readability layer:

- `static/css/dwrt-theme.css` owns semantic foreground tokens such as
  `--dwrt-ink`, `--dwrt-text`, `--dwrt-muted`, `--dwrt-faint`,
  `--dwrt-selected` and status text tokens.
- Entry pages should load `dwrt-theme.css` after page/component CSS so it can
  normalize foreground variables across app, setup and login surfaces.
- Page CSS should not hardcode neutral white/gray text colors. Use the shared
  `--dwrt-*`, `--app-text*`, `--dashboard-*`, `--dwrt-kit-*`, `--setup-*` or
  notification tokens. Hardcoded colors are allowed only for semantic accents,
  charts, icons and status indicators.
- Wallpaper-backed foreground is region-adaptive. Runtime code selects a
  near-black or near-white semantic pair from the actual wallpaper rectangle;
  theme mode is only a fallback and must not force one gray pair over the whole
  viewport.

Route modules:

- `static/js/menu-shell.js` is the central route gateway for `/app/#/...`.
- Dashboard, topology and other built-in shell pages may keep dedicated shared
  scripts while they are being migrated.
- Native and third-party plugin pages must be loaded from explicit menu
  manifest fields such as `module`, `route_module`, `plugin_module` or
  `plugin.resource`.
- Allowed plugin module resources are JavaScript files under
  `plugins/native/...` or `plugins/third-party/...`; absolute URLs, `..`,
  query strings and hash fragments are rejected by the route gateway.
- A plugin module should export either a default function or an object with
  `mount(ctx)`. It may return an object with `unmount()` for route cleanup.
- Runtime menu files under `dynamic/menu` should describe capabilities and
  module resources; route code should not hardcode installed plugin lists.
